    "q-70977": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70977",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $D(6,2,1)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨\\frac{1}{2},1,9⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and $r=⟨\\sqrt{3},10,-1⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨4,-1,5⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,2,3⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $D(6,2,1)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $d=⟨6,2,1⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =d+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨6,2,1⟩+s⟨4,-1,5⟩+t⟨0,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-70977-a",
